// Step 3.1f: Step, StepIn, StepOut, RunUntil, SetCurrentPC. Stepping sets
// temporary breakpoints, so breakpoints are enabled first.
// Work's bytecode: BreakLoop is called at pc 1 (PC 2 after it); pc 6 calls
// Add; pc 15 is BranchIfFalse for "y > 5" (to 26); 18-25 doubles y; 26
// pushes y; 27 returns.
// - Step: 2 -> 3. RunUntil(Work, 6): at the call. StepIn: Add's pc 0.
//   Step: Add's pc 1. StepOut: back in Work at 7, after the call.
// - RunUntil(Work, 15): the condition (true) is on the stack; Step decides
//   the branch is not taken: 18.
// - SetCurrentPC(26) skips the doubling: Work returns 11, not 22.
// - Step at 27 (return) stops in the caller, the script (not Work).
global Add(a, b)
begin
  a + b;
end;

global Work(x)
begin
  BreakLoop();
  local y := Add(x, 1);
  if y > 5 then y := y * 2;
  y;
end;

GloballyEnableBreakPoints(true);
Print(Work(10));
